{
  // Only the relay Worker (cloudflare/) is installed. The repository's site/
  // Worker is upstream's marketing site and download host, and the reminal
  // program itself is a Go binary people install on their own machines.
  "$schema": "https://appflare.github.io/catalog/schema/v1.json",
  "slug": "reminal",
  "name": "Reminal",
  "summary": "Your own relay for reminal: reach the terminals, app windows and desktops of your machines from any browser, end-to-end encrypted, with nothing listening on the machines.",
  "tagline": "Reach your computers' windows and terminals from any browser",
  "homepage": "https://reminal.app",
  "repo": "harshalgajjar/Reminal",
  "license": "AGPL-3.0-or-later",
  "categories": ["remote-access", "developer-tools"],
  "authors": [{ "name": "Harshal Gajjar", "github": "harshalgajjar" }],
  "maintainers": ["MendyLanda"],
  "source": { "ref": "v3.15.2", "sha": "d11ae7f0ca9c1590f1a7d35546d48f616114fe01" },
  "install": {
    "packageManager": "npm",
    "wranglerConfig": "cloudflare/wrangler.toml",
    // The relay is its own npm project with its own lockfile; the root is Go.
    "installDirs": [{ "path": "cloudflare" }],
    // The critical-upgrade beacon the reminal program polls; no sign-in.
    "health": { "path": "/version" }
  },
  // Two SQLite-backed Durable Object classes and static assets. Window and
  // desktop frames go peer-to-peer over WebRTC, so the relay carries only
  // terminal traffic and signalling.
  "plan": "free",
  "secrets": [
    {
      // Upstream reads the key as a JWK, which the install form cannot
      // generate, so phone alerts stay off until the admin pastes a pair.
      "name": "VAPID_PRIVATE_JWK",
      "label": "Alerts private key (JWK)",
      "help": "Turns on phone and desktop alerts: a P-256 VAPID private key as a JSON Web Key ({\"kty\":\"EC\",\"crv\":\"P-256\",\"d\":…,\"x\":…,\"y\":…}). Set the matching public key below too. Never change the pair once browsers have subscribed.",
      "optional": true
    }
  ],
  "vars": [
    {
      // The wrangler config carries upstream's own public key; without a
      // matching private key it would only advertise a key nobody here holds.
      "name": "VAPID_PUBLIC",
      "label": "Alerts public key",
      "help": "The public half of the alerts key, as unpadded base64url of the 65-byte uncompressed point. Leave it empty to keep alerts off.",
      "default": "",
      "optional": true
    }
  ],
  "postInstall": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Install the reminal program on each machine you want to reach (https://github.com/harshalgajjar/Reminal#set-it-up-in-one-line) and point it at this relay:\n\n```sh\nREMINAL_WEB={{appUrl}} reminal\n```\n\nIt prints a session ID, a PIN and a QR code; open the link on any device and enter the PIN."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "The relay has no accounts of its own. Each session is reachable only with the session ID and PIN the machine prints, or from a device you enrolled as an owner with `reminal own`. Terminal and window traffic is end-to-end encrypted. `reminal expose` port forwards are the exception: they serve a local web port at {{appUrl}}/p/<id>/ behind the PIN, and pass through this Worker unencrypted."
    }
  ]
}
